he study concludes that computer technology can enrich the creative experience of choreographers by p f o ~i d i n ~ new methods to explore movement compositionally and recommends further directions for choreographic research.'The Evolution of an Interface for Choreographers", Interchi proceedings, Interchi Conference, Amsterdam, Aprii 1993.Simon Fraser University, has been responsible for installing the LifeForms software In CunninghatrFssfudio in New Yoik, tutoring Cunningharn in its use, and supporting his creation and exploration of new movemefit with the LifeForms system.During ihe time that Cunningham has been using LifeForms, the author has travelled to New York to work with Cunningham on thirteen occasions and worked with Cunningham for a total of seventy five days, 1 he installation of the LifeForms chore~graphic software in Cunningham's Westbeth studio in New York city in December 1989, and the learning and creative piocess that ensued, has spanned a three year period as of this writing, T},
