  abstract = {This investigation which takes us through centuries points out the musical benefits obtained from the keyboard. Iconography, ancient musical reference books, teaching manuals, invention patents, collections of musical instruments, data processing and its musical applications were all used to identify and explore the functions developed from the principle of the keyboard and from the motion of the keys. The keyboard has long been included in many instruments, and exerted a fundamental influence on musical performance. All mechanical musical instruments, from the renaissance to the present day, ranging from the musical android to the player piano, have been designed and manufactured with the principle of the keyboard ; they all simulate the musical performance. As early as the 19th century, writing and reading keyboards could replicate and record a performance. Today, themidi interface and the sequencer, based upon the concept of the keyboard, allow the analysis of the inequalities in finger playing, as well as the elaboration of a grammar of keyboard playing. A consequence of this inquiry was the realization of a device for controlling musical expression called the ''digital master'' by the author. The conception and the realization of such an ''instrument'' were not conceivable without this research on the keyboard. The investigations performed on the ''musical keyboard'' and on the ''digital master'' emphasize the role of the keys. The keyboard is only a topographic landmark for},
