  abstract = {Trajectory information can be analysed in both the time and space dimensions via a new metric called the 7/t-metric. The 7/t-metric is a measurement definition which quantifies the allocation of control across multiple degrees of freedom. Allocation of control is defined as the product of two components, the simultaneity of control and the efficiency of control, corresponding to the time and space dimensions respectively. The existing human factors, biomedical, and motor control literature serves as the foundation for the development of the 7/t- metric. The 7/t-metric has several limitations including dependency upon the chosen coordinate system, assumptions of optimal trajectories, and the lack of frequency domain analysis.},
